From 9141e1d6bc0554ff2686bd4f6c277b785d0ff6f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Dawid=20Wr=C3=B3bel?= <me@dawidwrobel.com>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 10:21:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 15/41] tee: qseecom: unregister the device whose registration
 failed

The probe unwind jumped to the label that unregisters the client device when it
was the supplicant device that failed, leaking the allocated one. Unreachable
short of cdev_device_add() failing.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Assisted-by: Kimi:kimi-k3
---
 drivers/tee/qseecom/core.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/tee/qseecom/core.c b/drivers/tee/qseecom/core.c
index d074e26bf..f8d6eb772 100644
--- a/drivers/tee/qseecom/core.c
+++ b/drivers/tee/qseecom/core.c
@@ -1597,7 +1597,7 @@ static int qseecom_tee_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 	ret = tee_device_register(qtee->supp_teedev);
 	if (ret)
-		goto err_unreg_teedev;
+		goto err_unreg_supp_teedev;
 
 	platform_set_drvdata(pdev, qtee);
 
